  "body": "In Gecko, at least, the values get set from the `HTMLBodyElement`s attribute mapping code, which means that:\n\n * It doesn't run on disconnected elements.\n * Last body mutated wins.\n * There's some asynchronicities and exact order might even depend on hashtable iteration order.\n\nI think we should probably only support these attributes in [the body element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-body-element-2) of the document (if not a `frameset`), but would be good to know what Blink / WebKit do.\n\nGecko also doesn't deal with removals, but that's fixable.\n\ncc @annevk @whatwg/css ",
